# Website Typography

**Policy:** All site text uses the shared font system in `src/app/fonts.ts` and `globals.css`. Do not introduce ad-hoc font families.

## Font stack (single source of truth)

| Role | Implementation | Use for |
|------|----------------|---------|
| **Serif** | `Cormorant Garamond` → `--font-brand-serif` → `var(--brand-serif)` | Page titles, section headings, editorial leads, brand hero lines |
| **Sans** | `Source Sans 3` → `--font-brand-sans` → `var(--brand-sans)` | Body copy, UI, nav, tables, FAQ subheads, bullets, captions |

- Load fonts only via `next/font/google` in `src/app/fonts.ts` (`display: "swap"`, `subsets: ["latin"]`).
- Apply variables on `<html>` in `layout.tsx` — never add `<link>` tags for Google Fonts.
- Do **not** hardcode `Georgia`, `Helvetica Neue`, `Arial`, or other families in new CSS/inline styles.

## Role rules

```css
/* ✅ Serif — display / editorial */
font-family: var(--brand-serif);
font-weight: 500;   /* headings, leads */

/* ✅ Sans — reading / UI */
font-family: var(--brand-sans);
font-weight: 400;   /* body */
font-weight: 500;   /* labels, timeline steps, gallery captions */
font-weight: 600;   /* h3, table headers, emphasis */
```

- **Long-form body** (Stories, product copy): always sans, `line-height` 1.7–1.75, max-width ~38em.
- **Headings h1–h2**: serif weight 500. **h3 / FAQ / UI labels**: sans weight 600.
- **Tables**: `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` for spec/number columns.
- **Do not** mix a third font family without explicit user approval.

## Stories (`blog-article-*`)

Extend typography in `globals.css` under `.blog-article` — reuse `--blog-title`, `--blog-body`, `--blog-h2`, etc. Do not add per-article font overrides in `blogPosts.ts` or components.

| Element | Font | Weight |
|---------|------|--------|
| Title, lead, h2, closing | serif | 500 |
| Body, bullets, CTA desc | sans | 400 |
| h3 (FAQ), bullets-label | sans | 600 |
| Comparison captions | sans | 500 |

## When adding new pages or components

1. Inherit `body` sans — only add `var(--brand-serif)` for intentional display headings.
2. Prefer existing clamp scales in `globals.css`; add new tokens to `:root` or a scoped block, not magic `px` values.
3. Enable `text-rendering: optimizeLegibility` on long-reading containers only (already on `body`).
4. Run `npm run build` after font or typography changes.

## Checklist

- [ ] Uses `var(--brand-serif)` or `var(--brand-sans)` — no new font families
- [ ] Body/long copy is sans; display headings are serif
- [ ] New fonts (if ever needed) go in `fonts.ts` + `layout.tsx` + `:root` only
- [ ] Stories follow `blog-article-*` scale, not one-off sizes
